  "proof": "For finite centerlessG and S=C_G(a,c), the conjugation stabilizer ofb equals C_G(a,b,c). If the marks generateG, commuting with each mark means commuting with every element ofG, so this is Z(G)=1. Orbit-stabilizer gives orbit length|S|. Its contrapositive excludes genuine smallerS-orbits. Full-size orbits, setwiseT, subgroup orders, generation of surviving rows and reversal/IP do not follow.",
  "qualifications": [
    "Named centerlessG=A=Co2, actual mark membership, full pointwiseS12/order1280, normalized permutation/hash correctness and the complete/disjoint orbit interpretation remain imported accepted assumptions. Scalar/hash agreement alone does not establish them; positive_orbit_bijection_checked=false is retained.",
